## 1. CORE APPLICATION FLOW

Implement the following complete navigation flow.

Public visitor:
Landing Page → Login or Register → Authentication → Role-Based Dashboard

New customer:
Register → Validate Form → Create Account → Sign In or Automatically Authenticate → Customer Dashboard

Existing customer:
Login → Validate Credentials → Authenticate → Customer Dashboard

Administrator:
Login → Verify Administrator Role → Admin Dashboard

Customer actions:
Dashboard → Apply for Loan → Submit Application → Track Status → View Approved Loan → View EMI Schedule → Record Payment → View Payment History

Administrator actions:
Admin Dashboard → Manage Customers → Review Applications → Approve or Reject Loans → Manage Payments → View Reports → Manage Settings

Important:
- Every button, link, form, tab, dropdown, filter, and chart control must have a meaningful behavior.
- Protect authenticated routes.
- Redirect users according to their actual authenticated role.
- Customers must never access administrator-only pages or data.
- An administrator must not be created merely because someone selects "Admin" in the registration form.
- Do not implement authentication as a fake login that accepts any password.
- Do not show a dashboard before authentication succeeds.
- Preserve user sessions appropriately and handle logout correctly.
- Include useful loading, success, empty, and error states.

